    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "ROM 9:27",
        "textualBasisJa": "Isaiah cries concerning Israel, “If the number of the children of Israel are as the sand of the sea, it is the remnant who will be saved;"
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 9:29",
        "textualBasisJa": "As Isaiah has said before, “Unless the Lord of Armies had left us a seed, we would have become like Sodom, and would have been made like Gomorrah.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 10:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "But they didn’t all listen to the glad news. For Isaiah says, “Lord, who has believed our report?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 10:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "Isaiah is very bold and says, “I was found by those who didn’t seek me. I was revealed to those who didn’t ask for me.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 15:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "Again, Isaiah says, “There will be the root of Jesse, he who arises to rule over the Gentiles; in him the Gentiles will hope.”"
      }
    ],
